## The CSS

```css
/* ==========================================================================
   Blog Post Layout
   ========================================================================== */

/* --- Design Tokens --- */
:root {
  /* Typography */
  --font-serif: "Charter", "Bitstream Charter", "Sitka Text", Cambria, Georgia, serif;
  --font-sans: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;

  /* Fluid type scale */
  --text-sm: clamp(0.85rem, 0.82rem + 0.15vw, 0.925rem);
  --text-base: clamp(1.125rem, 1.08rem + 0.25vw, 1.25rem);
  --text-lg: clamp(1.4rem, 1.25rem + 0.75vw, 1.85rem);
  --text-xl: clamp(2.25rem, 1.8rem + 2.25vw, 3.5rem);

  /* Colors */
  --color-text: #1f2328;
  --color-text-muted: #5c6670;
  --color-heading: #111418;
  --color-accent: #b5472b;
  --color-border: #e3e6ea;
  --color-bg: #fdfcfa;
  --color-quote-bg: #f6f2ec;

  /* Layout */
  --measure: 68ch;
  --space-xs: 0.5rem;
  --space-sm: 1rem;
  --space-md: 1.5rem;
  --space-lg: 2.5rem;
  --space-xl: 4rem;
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --color-text: #d6d9dd;
    --color-text-muted: #9aa3ad;
    --color-heading: #f2f4f6;
    --color-accent: #e8825f;
    --color-border: #2e343b;
    --color-bg: #15181c;
    --color-quote-bg: #1e2227;
  }
}

/* --- Base --- */
body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--color-bg);
  color: var(--color-text);
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
}

/* --- Article Container --- */
.post {
  max-width: var(--measure);
  margin-inline: auto;
  padding: var(--space-xl) var(--space-md);
}

/* --- Header --- */
.post-header {
  margin-block-end: var(--space-lg);
  padding-block-end: var(--space-md);
  border-block-end: 1px solid var(--color-border);
}

/* --- Title --- */
.post-title {
  margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: var(--text-xl);
  font-weight: 700;
  line-height: 1.1;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  color: var(--color-heading);
  text-wrap: balance;
}

.post-subtitle {
  margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: var(--text-lg);
  font-weight: 400;
  line-height: 1.35;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
  text-wrap: balance;
}

/* --- Metadata Line --- */
.post-meta {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-xs);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: var(--text-sm);
  line-height: 1.4;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}

.post-meta li {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
}

/* Dot separators between items */
.post-meta li + li::before {
  content: "·";
  margin-inline-end: var(--space-xs);
  color: var(--color-border);
  font-weight: 700;
}

.post-meta a {
  color: var(--color-text);
  font-weight: 600;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.post-meta a:hover,
.post-meta a:focus-visible {
  color: var(--color-accent);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
}

.post-meta .tag {
  padding: 0.15em 0.6em;
  border-radius: 999px;
  background: var(--color-quote-bg);
  color: var(--color-accent);
  font-size: 0.85em;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

/* --- Body Text --- */
.post-body {
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: var(--text-base);
  line-height: 1.7;
  hyphens: auto;
  overflow-wrap: break-word;
}

.post-body > * {
  margin-block: 0;
}

/* Consistent vertical rhythm */
.post-body > * + * {
  margin-block-start: var(--space-md);
}

.post-body p {
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* Drop cap on the first paragraph */
.post-body > p:first-of-type::first-letter {
  float: left;
  margin: 0.08em 0.12em 0 0;
  font-size: 3.6em;
  font-weight: 700;
  line-height: 0.8;
  color: var(--color-accent);
}

.post-body h2,
.post-body h3 {
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  color: var(--color-heading);
  line-height: 1.25;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  text-wrap: balance;
}

.post-body h2 {
  margin-block-start: var(--space-xl);
  font-size: var(--text-lg);
}

.post-body h3 {
  margin-block-start: var(--space-lg);
  font-size: 1.15em;
}

/* Tighten space between a heading and the text it introduces */
.post-body :is(h2, h3) + * {
  margin-block-start: var(--space-sm);
}

.post-body a {
  color: var(--color-accent);
  text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
}

.post-body a:hover {
  text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
}

.post-body ul,
.post-body ol {
  padding-inline-start: 1.5em;
}

.post-body li + li {
  margin-block-start: var(--space-xs);
}

.post-body img {
  display: block;
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
  border-radius: 4px;
}

.post-body code {
  padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
  border-radius: 3px;
  background: var(--color-quote-bg);
  font-size: 0.875em;
}

/* --- Pull Quotes --- */
.pull-quote {
  position: relative;
  margin-block: var(--space-lg);
  padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-md) var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
  border-inline-start: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
  background: var(--color-quote-bg);
  border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
}

/* Decorative opening quote mark */
.pull-quote::before {
  content: "\201C";
  position: absolute;
  top: -0.15em;
  left: 0.15em;
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: 4.5em;
  line-height: 1;
  color: var(--color-accent);
  opacity: 0.2;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.pull-quote p {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: var(--text-lg);
  font-style: italic;
  font-weight: 500;
  line-height: 1.4;
  color: var(--color-heading);
  text-wrap: balance;
}

.pull-quote cite {
  display: block;
  margin-block-start: var(--space-sm);
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: var(--text-sm);
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}

.pull-quote cite::before {
  content: "— ";
}

/* Floated variant: pulls out to the side on wide screens */
@media (min-width: 64rem) {
  .pull-quote--aside {
    float: right;
    width: 45%;
    margin: var(--space-xs) calc(-1 * var(--space-xl)) var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
    padding: var(--space-sm) 0;
    border: none;
    border-block: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: 0;
    background: none;
  }

  .pull-quote--aside::before {
    display: none;
  }

  .pull-quote--aside p {
    font-size: 1.35em;
  }
}

/* --- Print --- */
@media print {
  .post {
    max-width: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .post-body {
    font-size: 11pt;
  }

  .pull-quote {
    break-inside: avoid;
    background: none;
  }

  .post-body a::after {
    content: " (" attr(href) ")";
    font-size: 0.8em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
}
```

## Example HTML

```html
<article class="post">
  <header class="post-header">
    <h1 class="post-title">The Quiet Art of Typography</h1>
    <p class="post-subtitle">Why the best design is the kind you never notice.</p>

    <ul class="post-meta">
      <li>By <a href="/authors/jane">Jane Doe</a></li>
      <li><time datetime="2024-06-12">June 12, 2024</time></li>
      <li>8 min read</li>
      <li><span class="tag">Design</span></li>
    </ul>
  </header>

  <div class="post-body">
    <p>Good typography is invisible. When it works, readers move through the text without friction...</p>

    <p>Consider line length. Somewhere between 45 and 75 characters per line...</p>

    <blockquote class="pull-quote">
      <p>Typography exists to honor content.</p>
      <cite>Robert Bringhurst</cite>
    </blockquote>

    <h2>Rhythm and Spacing</h2>
    <p>Vertical rhythm gives a page its sense of calm...</p>

    <aside class="pull-quote pull-quote--aside" aria-hidden="true">
      <p>Whitespace is not empty space. It is structure.</p>
    </aside>

    <p>More body text continues here...</p>
  </div>
</article>
```

## Design Notes

**Readability**
- **68ch max width** keeps lines in the ideal 45–75 character range.
- **1.7 line height** gives body text room to breathe.
- **Fluid type** via `clamp()` scales smoothly from mobile to desktop without breakpoints.

**Typography details**
- `text-wrap: balance` on headings prevents awkward single-word last lines.
- `text-wrap: pretty` on paragraphs reduces orphans (progressive enhancement).
- A drop cap on the first paragraph adds an editorial touch. Delete that rule if you don't want it.

**Two pull quote styles**
- `.pull-quote` is an inline, full-width block with an accent bar. Use it for real quotations from a source.
- `.pull-quote--aside` floats into the margin on wide screens, magazine-style. Use it for excerpts repeated from the article itself. Mark it `aria-hidden="true"` so screen readers don't read the text twice.

**Extras**
- Automatic dark mode via `prefers-color-scheme`.
- Print styles that remove backgrounds and show link URLs.
- All colors and spacing live in CSS custom properties, so retheming means changing a few variables.

