## Key Design Decisions

| Element | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Line length** | `68ch` max | Optimal readability is 60–75 characters per line |
| **Body line-height** | `1.7` | Generous spacing helps long-form reading |
| **Title** | Tight `1.12` line-height, negative tracking | Large text needs tighter spacing to look cohesive |
| **Metadata** | Sans-serif, small, muted | Visually separates "info about" from "content" |
| **Pull quotes** | Larger italic serif + accent border | Breaks up text and draws the eye without clutter |
| **Fluid type** | `clamp()` | Scales smoothly from mobile to desktop, no breakpoints needed |
| **`text-wrap: balance`** | Titles and quotes | Prevents awkward single-word last lines |

The pull quote floats into the right margin on wide screens (magazine-style) and stays inline on smaller ones. Remove the drop cap block if you prefer a simpler look.

