## Key Design Decisions

| Element | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Line length** | `68ch` max-width | 60–75 characters per line is the readability sweet spot |
| **Title** | `clamp()` + `text-wrap: balance` | Scales fluidly and avoids lopsided line breaks |
| **Metadata** | Sans-serif, muted, auto dot separators | Visually secondary to the title; separators come from CSS, not markup |
| **Body** | Serif at ~18–20px, `line-height: 1.7` | Comfortable for long-form reading |
| **Pull quotes** | Accent border, tinted background, large italic text | Breaks up long text and draws the eye without overwhelming the page |
| **Theming** | CSS custom properties + dark mode | Easy to rebrand in one place |

**Tip:** Add the class `pull-quote--aside` (e.g., `class="pull-quote pull-quote--aside"`) to float a quote into the right margin on large screens, magazine-style. Since pull quotes repeat text from the article, you may also want to add `aria-hidden="true"` to them so screen readers don't read the content twice.

