## Key Design Decisions

| Element | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Line length** | `68ch` max width | Sits in the 45–75 character range, which is easiest to read |
| **Body line-height** | `1.7` | Generous spacing for long-form reading |
| **Title sizing** | `clamp()` | Scales fluidly from mobile to desktop without breakpoints |
| **Metadata** | Sans-serif, muted, smaller | Visually subordinate to the title, with contrast against the serif body |
| **Separators** | CSS `::before` dots | No extra markup, and they wrap cleanly |
| **Pull quotes** | Larger italic serif with an accent border | Clearly distinct from body text without being garish |
| **`text-wrap`** | `balance` / `pretty` | Better line breaks in modern browsers and ignored by older ones |

**Variant:** Add `class="pull-quote pull-quote--aside"` to make a quote float into the right margin on wide screens, like in a magazine layout.

