## Key Design Decisions

| Feature | Why |
|---|---|
| **68ch max-width** | Keeps lines at ~60–75 characters, the optimal range for readability |
| **`clamp()` font sizes** | Scales smoothly from mobile to desktop without breakpoints |
| **Sans title / serif body** | Classic contrast: headings feel modern, body text reads comfortably |
| **`line-height: 1.7`** | Generous leading for long-form reading |
| **`text-wrap: balance/pretty`** | Prevents awkward title breaks and orphaned words (progressive enhancement) |
| **Pseudo-element separators** | Metadata dots are added with CSS, so the HTML stays clean |
| **Breakout pull quotes** | Extending past the text column on wide screens adds visual rhythm |
| **CSS variables + dark mode** | Easy theming, with automatic support for the user's system preference |

You can remove the drop cap rule if you prefer a simpler opening, or swap in the `--centered` pull quote variant for a more magazine-style look.

