## Key Design Decisions

| Feature | Why |
|---|---|
| **`68ch` max-width** | Keeps lines in the 60–75 character range, which is most comfortable to read |
| **`clamp()` font sizes** | Scales typography smoothly between mobile and desktop without breakpoints |
| **Serif body / sans meta** | Serif aids long-form reading; sans-serif distinguishes UI elements like metadata |
| **`line-height: 1.7`** | Generous leading for body text; tighter (1.15) for the large title |
| **`text-wrap: balance/pretty`** | Prevents awkward headline breaks and orphaned words (progressive enhancement) |
| **CSS custom properties** | Makes theming and dark mode a simple variable swap |
| **Breakout pull quotes** | Extend past the column on wide screens for visual emphasis |

If you'd prefer a more minimal pull quote (centered, no background, top/bottom rules), swap the `.pull-quote` block for this:

```css
