## Key Design Decisions

| Element | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Line length** | `68ch` max width | 60–75 characters per line is the readability sweet spot |
| **Title** | `clamp()` sizing, tight leading, `text-wrap: balance` | Scales fluidly; prevents awkward one-word last lines |
| **Metadata** | Sans-serif, smaller, muted, dot separators via `::before` | Visually subordinate to the title; separators don't clutter the HTML |
| **Body** | Serif, `line-height: 1.7`, `text-wrap: pretty` | Generous leading for long-form reading; avoids orphans |
| **Pull quote** | Larger italic serif, accent border, faint oversized quote mark | Breaks up long text and draws the eye without overwhelming |
| **Dark mode** | Token swap via `prefers-color-scheme` | Respects user settings with no extra classes |

**Tip:** Add the `pull-quote--aside` modifier class (`<blockquote class="pull-quote pull-quote--aside">`) for a floated, magazine-style quote that hangs into the right margin on wide screens.

