# Blog Post Layout CSS

## HTML Structure (for reference)

```html
<article class="blog-post">
  <header class="post-header">
    <h1 class="post-title">The Art of Slow Reading</h1>
    <div class="post-meta">
      <span class="meta-author">By Jane Doe</span>
      <time class="meta-date" datetime="2025-01-15">January 15, 2025</time>
      <span class="meta-reading-time">6 min read</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="post-body">
    <p>Body text goes here...</p>

    <blockquote class="pull-quote">
      <p>Reading slowly is not a failure of comprehension, but an act of devotion.</p>
      <cite>— Marcel Proust</cite>
    </blockquote>

    <p>More body text...</p>
  </div>
</article>
```

## CSS

```css
/* ---------------------------------------
   Blog Post Layout
--------------------------------------- */

.blog-post {
  /* Constrain line length for readability (~65–75 characters) */
  max-width: 42rem;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem;
}

/* ---------- Title ---------- */

.post-title {
  font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
  line-height: 1.15;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  margin: 0 0 1rem;
}

/* ---------- Metadata Line ---------- */

.post-meta {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  align-items: center;
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  color: #6b6b6b;
  padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 2rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5;
}

.post-meta > * + *::before {
  content: "•";
  margin-right: 0.75rem;
  color: #c0c0c0;
}

.meta-author {
  font-weight: 600;
  color: #444;
}

/* ---------- Body Text ---------- */

.post-body {
  font-size: 1.0625rem;          /* ~17px */
  line-height: 1.75;
  color: #2d2d2d;
}

.post-body p {
  margin: 0 0 1.5em;
}

.post-body h2 {
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  line-height: 1.3;
  margin: 2.5em 0 0.75em;
  color: #1a1a1a;
}

.post-body a {
  color: #0b5fff;
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 3px;
}

.post-body a:hover {
  color: #0847c7;
}

/* ---------- Pull Quotes ---------- */

.pull-quote {
  margin: 2.5rem 0;
  padding: 0 0 0 1.5rem;
  border-left: 4px solid #0b5fff;
}

.pull-quote p {
  font-size: 1.375rem;
  line-height: 1.45;
  font-style: italic;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
}

.pull-quote cite {
  display: block;
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  font-style: normal;
  color: #6b6b6b;
}

/* ---------- Responsive Tweaks ---------- */

@media (min-width: 48rem) {
  .blog-post {
    padding: 3rem 2rem 5rem;
  }

  /* Let pull quotes break the text column slightly */
  .pull-quote {
    margin-left: -1.5rem;
    margin-right: -1.5rem;
  }
}
```

## Key Design Decisions

- **`max-width: 42rem`** — keeps body text at a comfortable reading measure (~65–75 characters per line).
- **`clamp()` on the title** — fluid typography that scales with viewport without media queries.
- **Separator dots via `::before`** — metadata items are joined with bullets without extra markup.
- **Negative margins on pull quotes** — on wider screens, quotes visually "pull" outside the text column for emphasis.
- **Generous `line-height: 1.75`** — improves long-form readability.

