### Layout & Visual Design

The page is built around a single article container with a comfortable reading measure and a warm, editorial feel. Here's what stands out:

- **Typography & rhythm** – The title uses a fluid `clamp()` size that scales smoothly from mobile to desktop, while the body text stays at a readable 68ch line length. The metadata line is set in a smaller, uppercase sans-serif with dot separators between items.
- **Pull quote variations** – There are two pull quote styles: a centered block with top and bottom borders, and a floated variant that sits to the right on wider screens. Both use italic serif type and an accent color to draw the eye.
- **Dark mode support** – CSS custom properties automatically switch the color palette when the user's system prefers dark mode, keeping contrast comfortable without extra markup.
- **Responsive behavior** – The layout uses `clamp()` for spacing and font sizes, and the floated pull quote only appears at 48rem and above, so the reading experience stays clean on smaller screens.
