### Layout and Visual Rhythm

The page uses a centered article shell with a max width that keeps line lengths comfortable for reading. The title scales up on larger screens with a balanced text wrap, while the metadata line stays compact and uppercase with a subtle middot separator. Body paragraphs use soft spacing and a slightly tightened line height, and links are underlined with an accent color that matches the pull quote. Pull quotes can appear as a left-bordered block, a centered statement, or a floating callout on wider screens, with an optional decorative quote mark for extra emphasis.
