### Design Choices for the Blog Post Layout

The stylesheet uses a few deliberate moves to keep the reading experience calm and clear.

- **Typography rhythm** – The title uses `clamp()` for fluid scaling and `text-wrap: balance` to even out headline lines. Body text is set to a comfortable 68ch measure with `text-wrap: pretty` to avoid orphan words.
- **Metadata separators** – Dots between author, date, and read time are generated with a pseudo-element, keeping the HTML clean while maintaining a subtle visual rhythm.
- **Pull quote variants** – The default quote floats right so body copy wraps around it, while the centered variant breaks the column with top and bottom borders. Both use a serif italic style and a muted accent color to signal quotation without shouting.
- **Small screens** – On narrower viewports the float is removed, letting pull quotes span the full column for easier reading.
---

**Optimization Tip:** You can swap the accent color in `:root` (currently `#b45309`) to match your brand, and adjust the pull quote width via `min(42%, 17rem)`.

