### Blog Post Layout: Core Modules

This layout keeps the reading experience clean and focused, with each part doing a clear job.

- **Title** – Uses a serif display font with fluid sizing and balanced line breaks, so headlines stay readable at any width.
- **Metadata line** – A flex row with uppercase text and dot separators, showing author, date, and reading time in a compact, scannable format.
- **Body text** – A comfortable measure (70ch) and generous line height, with automatic spacing between paragraphs for easy reading.
- **Pull quotes** – Floated right or left variants sit beside the text, while a centered full-width variant breaks the flow for emphasis. All collapse to full-width on small screens and in print.

