### Blog Post Layout & Typography

This layout uses a clean, readable structure with a few thoughtful touches to keep long-form content comfortable.

- **Title & metadata:** The title scales fluidly with `clamp()`, while the metadata line uses uppercase, letter-spaced text with dot separators between items.
- **Body text:** A serif font at 1.125rem with a 68ch measure keeps paragraphs easy on the eyes. The first paragraph is slightly larger to draw readers in.
- **Pull quotes:** Three variants are available — default centered, floated to the right, and full-bleed breakout. Each uses a decorative opening quotation mark and an optional citation.
- **Dark mode:** Colors switch automatically based on the user's system preference, so the layout stays legible in both light and dark environments.
---

**Optimization Tip:** You can replace the sample title, author, date, and pull quote text in the HTML with your own content. The `--post-measure` variable controls the reading width, and `--post-accent` changes the pull quote color.

