### Blog Post Layout Modules

This CSS covers the main building blocks of a blog post, from the header down to the pull quotes.

- **Title & metadata header** – The post title uses fluid typography with balanced line wrapping, while the metadata line arranges author, date, and reading time with dot separators and a subtle bottom border.
- **Body text flow** – Paragraphs, headings, lists, and images share a consistent vertical rhythm, with `text-wrap: pretty` reducing orphaned words and links styled in the accent color.
- **Pull quotes** – Two pull quote variants are included: a centered break quote with a colored left border, and a floated variant that sits to the right on wider screens, falling back to the centered style on mobile.
- **Supporting elements** – Regular blockquotes, horizontal rules, and responsive small-screen adjustments are also defined for complete post styling.
---

**Optimization Tip:** You can adjust the reading width and vertical spacing by modifying the `--measure` and `--flow` variables in the `:root` block. The accent color and dark-mode palette are also defined there for quick rebranding.

