### Header Layout & Responsive Behavior

The header is built as a flexible three-part bar: brand, navigation, and actions. On desktop, the logo, nav links, and buttons sit on one row with comfortable spacing. The logo uses an inline SVG icon and text, while the nav links get an animated underline on hover or keyboard focus. The primary button uses the accent color and a pill shape, and the ghost button provides a subtler secondary action.

On smaller screens, the nav links disappear and a hamburger menu button appears, with the ghost button hidden on very narrow screens to save space. The header itself sticks to the top and uses a translucent background with a blur effect, so content scrolling underneath remains slightly visible.
---

**Optimization Tip:** The mobile menu button is included, but its dropdown panel isn't implemented yet — you can add JavaScript to toggle a nav drawer when the button is clicked.

