### Header Layout & Responsive Behavior

The header stays usable on any screen size, with a few thoughtful touches that make it feel polished.

- **Sticky glass header** – The header sticks to the top of the viewport and uses a subtle blur and translucent background, so content scrolls behind it without losing readability.
- **Desktop navigation** – Logo, nav links, and the CTA button sit in a single row. Links have a smooth color change and an animated underline on hover, while the CTA button lifts slightly with a soft shadow.
- **Mobile menu** – Below 860px, the nav links collapse into a hamburger toggle. The three bars animate into an X when opened, and the menu drops down as a full-width panel with stacked links and the CTA button.
- **Accessibility & motion** – Focus outlines are visible for keyboard users, and all transitions are reduced to near-zero for people who prefer less motion.
---

**Optimization Tip:** You can replace the placeholder `#` hrefs with your real page URLs, and update the logo SVG path or brand name to match your own site.

