### Header Layout & Interaction Highlights

The header keeps navigation clear and accessible across screen sizes.

- **Sticky, blurred header:** stays at the top of the viewport with a subtle backdrop blur and bottom border, so it remains visible while scrolling.
- **Flexible navigation:** the logo, nav links, and action buttons are arranged with flexbox, keeping spacing consistent and adapting gracefully to narrower widths.
- **Mobile dropdown menu:** below 860px, the nav links collapse into a dropdown panel toggled by a hamburger button. The button animates into an “X” when expanded.
- **Accessible focus states:** all interactive elements show a visible focus ring, and a skip link lets keyboard users jump straight to the main content.
- **Reduced motion support:** animations are minimized for users who prefer less motion, following accessibility best practices.
---

**Optimization Tip:** You can replace the placeholder logo SVG and the `#` href values with your actual brand assets and page URLs. The color tokens in `:root` are also easy to adjust to match your site's palette.

