**A few notes on the choices:**

- **`--measure: 68ch`** keeps line length in the 60–75 character range, which is the sweet spot for comfortable reading. Change it once to retune the whole layout.
- **`text-wrap: balance`** on the title and pull quotes prevents orphaned words on the last line — supported in modern browsers, ignored safely elsewhere.
- **The drop cap** is scoped to `p:first-of-type` so it only applies to the opening paragraph; remove that rule if you don't want it.
- **Meta separators** use `::before` on all but the first child, so adding or removing items never breaks the dot spacing.
- **Dark mode** is token-driven — swap the custom properties and everything else follows.

