      <p>Speed is a feature, but only when it doesn't cost you the user's trust.</p>
      <cite>Jane Doe</cite>
    </blockquote>

    <p>More text…</p>
  </div>

  <footer class="post-footer">
    <ul class="post-tags">
      <li><a href="/tag/design">Design</a></li>
      <li><a href="/tag/performance">Performance</a></li>
    </ul>
  </footer>
</article>
```

**Key design decisions:**
- **Measure capped at `42rem`** (~65–70 characters) for comfortable reading.
- **Fluid title** via `clamp()` so it scales from phone to desktop.
- **Metadata separated by `::before` dots** — no extra markup needed, and it wraps gracefully.
- **Pull quotes** come in three variants: `-left` (default), `--centered`, `--highlight`.
- **`text-wrap: balance`** on headings and quotes to avoid ragged lines.
- Dark mode and print styles included for real-world use.

