## CSS

```css
/* =========================================================
   Blog post layout
   ========================================================= */

/* ---------- Design tokens ---------- */
:root {
  --font-sans: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto,
               "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  --font-serif: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, Georgia,
                "Times New Roman", serif;

  --color-bg: #fbfaf8;
  --color-surface: #ffffff;
  --color-text: #1c1b1a;
  --color-text-muted: #5f5c57;
  --color-accent: #9a3412;
  --color-rule: #e4e0d9;

  --measure: 68ch;          /* max line length */
  --gutter: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  --radius: 6px;
}

/* ---------- Reset (scoped essentials) ---------- */
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  background: var(--color-bg);
  color: var(--color-text);
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.97rem + 0.15vw, 1.125rem);
  line-height: 1.65;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

/* =========================================================
   Article shell
   ========================================================= */
.post {
  max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--gutter));
  margin-inline: auto;
  padding: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem) var(--gutter);
}

/* ---------- Header ---------- */
.post__header {
  margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  text-align: center;
}

.post__title {
  margin: 0 0 1rem;
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.4rem + 3vw, 3.25rem);
  font-weight: 700;
  line-height: 1.1;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  text-wrap: balance;          /* avoids orphans in the headline */
}

/* Optional eyebrow / category label */
.post__eyebrow {
  display: inline-block;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--color-accent);
}

/* ---------- Metadata line ---------- */
.post__meta {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  line-height: 1.4;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}

.post__meta > * + *::before {
  content: "·";
  margin-right: 1rem;
  color: var(--color-rule);
}

.post__author { font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text); }
.post__meta a { color: inherit; text-decoration-color: var(--color-rule); }
.post__meta a:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }

/* ---------- Body ---------- */
.post__body > * + * {
  margin-top: 1.25em;
}

.post__body p {
  margin: 0;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* Lede / standfirst */
.post__lede {
  font-size: 1.25em;
  line-height: 1.5;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
  font-style: italic;
}

/* Optional drop cap on the first paragraph of the article */
.post__lede::first-letter,
.post__body > p:first-of-type::first-letter {
  float: left;
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: 3.4em;
  font-weight: 700;
  line-height: 0.82;
  padding: 0.06em 0.08em 0 0;
  color: var(--color-accent);
}

/* Headings inside the body */
.post__body h2,
.post__body h3 {
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  line-height: 1.25;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  margin-top: 2.25em;
  margin-bottom: 0.6em;
  text-wrap: balance;
}
.post__body h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 1.2rem + 0.8vw, 1.85rem); }
.post__body h3 { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.05rem + 0.5vw, 1.4rem); }

/* Links */
.post__body a {
  color: var(--color-accent);
  text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
}
.post__body a:hover { text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }

/* Lists, code, media */
.post__body ul,
.post__body ol { padding-left: 1.35em; }
.post__body li + li { margin-top: 0.4em; }

.post__body img,
.post__body video {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  display: block;
  margin-inline: auto;
}

.post__body figure { margin: 2em 0; }
.post__body figcaption {
  margin-top: 0.6rem;
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: 0.85rem;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
  text-align: center;
}

.post__body pre {
  overflow-x: auto;
  padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
  background: var(--color-surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  line-height: 1.55;
}
.post__body :not(pre) > code {
  font-size: 0.875em;
  background: var(--color-surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
}

/* =========================================================
   Pull quotes
   ========================================================= */
.pull-quote {
  margin: 2.5em 0;
  padding: 1.5em 0 1.5em 1.5em;
  border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
}

.pull-quote p {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1.05rem + 1vw, 1.65rem);
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.3;
  letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  text-wrap: balance;
}

.pull-quote cite {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 0.85rem;
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}

/* Alternate variant: centered, top/bottom rules */
.pull-quote--center {
  border-left: 0;
  padding: 2em 1em;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  text-align: center;
}
.pull-quote--center p { font-style: italic; font-weight: 500; }

/* Large "callout" quote spanning wider than the text column */
.pull-quote--feature {
  margin-inline: calc(50% - 50vw);
  padding-inline: var(--gutter);
  border-left: 0;
  text-align: center;
  background: var(--color-surface);
  border-block: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
}

/* =========================================================
   Footer / tags
   ========================================================= */
.post__footer {
  margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
  padding-top: 1.5rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
}

.post__tags {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}
.post__tags li {
  padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  border-radius: 999px;
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}

/* =========================================================
   Dark mode
   ========================================================= */
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --color-bg: #14161a;
    --color-surface: #1c1f25;
    --color-text: #e8e6e3;
    --color-text-muted: #a3a09b;
    --color-accent: #fb923c;
    --color-rule: #2c3038;
  }
}

/* =========================================================
   Responsive tweaks
   ========================================================= */
@media (max-width: 30rem) {
  .post__meta {
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }
  .post__meta > * + *::before { content: none; }

  .pull-quote {
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left-width: 3px;
  }
}

/* =========================================================
   Accessibility & print
   ========================================================= */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  * { animation: none !important; transition: none !important; }
}

@media print {
  body { background: #fff; color: #000; font-size: 11pt; }
  .post { max-width: none; padding: 0; }
  .pull-quote { border-left-color: #000; }
  .post__footer { display: none; }
}
```

### Quick notes on choices

- **`text-wrap: balance` / `pretty`** — modern CSS that fixes headline orphans and ragged last lines in body copy.
- **`clamp()` everywhere** — the layout scales fluidly without a pile of media queries.
- **Drop cap** — applied via `::first-letter`; remove the rule if you don't want it, and note it doesn't work on `display: flex` elements.
- **Pull quotes** — three variants: default (left rule), `--center`, and `--feature` (full-bleed via `margin-inline: calc(50% - 50vw)`).
- **Dark mode** — token swap only; no duplicated rules.
- **Measure of `68ch`** — roughly 70–80 characters, the comfortable reading range. Adjust `--measure` to taste.

